cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  restore-rsi: auditing the selection gate of a self-improving
  image-restoration agent
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Pengtao
repository-code: https://github.com/huangpengtao00-dotcom/restore-rsi
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-09-06'
keywords:
  - self-improving agents
  - agent evaluation
  - reward model reliability
  - image restoration
  - negative results
abstract: >-
  A JarvisIR-style image-restoration toolbox wired into reef's harness-evolution
  loop, and a measurement of the loop's own evaluation machinery. Three findings:
  the stock selection rule ("more wins than losses") has a 50% false-positive
  rate independent of repeats, so none of the skills it published survive a sign
  test; the diagnosis and reward defects that looked like policy noise are
  fixable and their repair moves tool usage toward the optimal chains; and the
  real bottleneck is knowing when to stop, worth 23% of the reachable score,
  with a ten-line deterministic greedy rule outperforming the LLM agent on every
  evaluation task while never collapsing to zero. CPU-only, no GPU.
